report.summary:
WP-35: all three findings are fixed, and every check passes.

BLOCKER (number literals reached jsonschema/v6 unbounded). Fixed with approach (a), the value-equivalent surrogate. No new refusal, and diagnostics are byte-identical.
- New file internal/config/schemaview/numbers.go holds the number model. Its header lists every place jsonschema/v6 v6.0.3 reads a number value:
  - isInteger (type integer);
  - numValidate (minimum, maximum, exclusiveMinimum, exclusiveMaximum, multipleOf);
  - equals (const, enum, and uniqueItems up to 20 items);
  - writeHash (uniqueItems above 20 items);
  - objCompiler.numVal and intVal at compile time.
  typeOf reads only the Go type, formats are annotations, and the vocabulary's Validate reads nothing.
- Compile builds the model from the view before compiling it. The grid is every multiple of 10^-F with magnitude below 10^I, where I and F are at least 40 and cover every number in the view. The period Q is the lcm of 10^F and each multipleOf value times 10^F, factored as 2^x 5^y times a coprime part. Compile refuses a view (ErrSchema) whose numbers need more than 400 digits or whose period exceeds 400 digits.
- work.instance, the only builder of the validator's instance, calls numberModel.bound on every KindInt and KindFloat node:
  - a literal on the grid of at most 64 bytes passes as written;
  - a longer literal on the grid passes in normalized form;
  - any other literal gets a bounded surrogate.
  The surrogate is off the grid, on the same side of every grid point, with the literal's integrality and multipleOf divisibility (exact residue mod Q for small shifts, a pattern residue for large ones). In a view with uniqueItems it gets an exact-value tag, so equal values share a surrogate and distinct values do not.
- Long literals charge their bytes as work units while being read or copied, 256 at a time, so Yield fires inside them. This includes the grammar scan, the mantissa reduction mod the coprime part, and the key copy with a reversed-digit exponent sum.
- validate() wraps sch.Validate with a recover. A library panic becomes RZ-CFG-005 "cannot be validated: the schema validator failed" at the root, without the value.
- A number node whose text is outside RFC 8259 (excluded by the tree contract) skips the validator. It is reported as RZ-CFG-005 "cannot be validated: a number is not an RFC 8259 number literal" at the node's position.
- The Options, package, Validate and Compile docs now state the validator's per-number cost bound and the three spans that cannot yield.

Class members covered, each with its own tests:
- numValidate minimum, maximum, exclusiveMinimum, exclusiveMaximum and multipleOf (3, 0.3, 0.25, 7.5);
- isInteger (listener port);
- equals for enum, const and nested const;
- uniqueItems pairwise (up to 20 items) and hash (above 20 items);
- the anyOf integer branches (ByteSize, IntOrString) and the oneOf integer branch;
- traceSampling, failureRatio and similarityThreshold;
- exponents 1e999999, 1e-999999, 1e1000001, 1e-1000001 and -1E+9999999999, and exponents of more than 18 digits;
- a 1 MiB mantissa, fractions of 1M and 2M digits, a 1M-digit integer, and long exact and long near-bound literals;
- both front ends (profile YAML and JSON), and a ${VAR} re-typed by subst;
- FuzzValidate seeds;
- the compile-time numVal path;
- the recover backstop and invalid text.

MAJOR (diagnostics cap). Options.MaxDiagnostics is added, following the profile, overlay, subst and defaults convention: zero or less means the MaxDiagnostics default. The mapper keeps cap+1 (the field is renamed limit to keep), so prune and result return the first cap+1 in sorted order. Existing truncation and scale tests now use the cap+1 contract.

MINOR. The memo comment in locate.go and the prefixBudget comment in scale_test.go now describe the mechanism (about log2(k) entries or bytes per diagnostic, run-to-run variation from map order). The memo comment now says "compareEntries compares (the sort and the bound check in mapper.record)".

report.checks:
Scoped checks, all green on the final tree:
- go build ./internal/config/schemaview/...
- go vet, with and without the integration tag
- go test -race -count=1 -cover -shuffle=on: ok, 98.2% coverage (numbers.go is 100% except the walk-error lines, which are covered too)
- CGO_ENABLED=0 go test -count=1: ok
- go test -tags integration: ok. The JSON Schema Test Suite passes, and a new TestJSONSchemaTestSuiteNumbers re-runs 406 suite cases with 544 surrogates, every result as expected.
- bin/golangci-lint fmt and run, with and without the integration tag: 0 issues
- go run ./internal/tool/repocheck: ok
- Fuzzing, each target over 60 s: FuzzValidate (1.7M execs, new seeds plus a property that bounded and as-written diagnostics agree when literals are quick) and FuzzNumberBound (big.Rat oracle on literal pairs). Both PASS.

New tests:
- TestParseLiteral, TestExponentKey, TestNumberModel (including Compile refusals and model-before-compile order);
- TestBoundOracle: exact big.Rat oracle for order against every view number, integrality, multipleOf divisibility, off-grid, size, exponent and injectivity, over 3,000+ literals and 4 models;
- TestHugeNumberLiterals: 20 huge literals × 6 rendered positions, diagnostics equal to the short equivalent, plus a handed-number check of bytes and exponent;
- TestHugeNumbersView: 10 literals × 12 synthetic keyword fields, enum and const included;
- TestValidateNumbersDifferential: bounded vs as-written diagnostics on the numbers view and the rendered view;
- TestUniqueItemsNumbers: pairwise and hash, carry and borrow in huge exponents;
- TestNumberWorkBounded: counters only, no clocks. 400 surrogates, retained big.Rat bits at most 512 each, yields at least len/256 inside 1 and 2 MiB mantissas, exact unit totals;
- TestNumberCharges, TestValidatorPanicRecovered, TestInvalidNumberText, TestNumberFrontEnds (YAML, JSON, subst), TestConcurrentNumberModel;
- TestMaxDiagnosticsOption (caps 1 and 7 at n = c-1, c, c+1, 2c+1, 2c+2, 5c+3; zero and negative caps);
- TestCollectorCapSignal (diag.Collector(10000): RZ-CFG-001 at 10001 and 15000 findings, none at 9999 or 10000; cap 7: at 8 and 30, none at 7).

Overlay proof against the pre-fix code (all .go files restored from a baseline copy, new files removed, proof file zz_proof_test.go added):
- Every proof test fails before the fix and passes after.
- TestZZBounded: panics at traceSampling, failureRatio and similarityThreshold; wrong "must be an integer" diagnostics at port, ByteSize and IntOrString for 1e1000001 and -1E+9999999999.
- TestZZFraction2M: panic.
- TestZZCost: 132,877,040 retained bits; 0 yields in a 1 MiB literal.
- TestZZNumbersView: range, open, third, tenth, quarter and step fail before the fix (panics or wrong diagnostics).
- TestZZUnique: pairwise misses the duplicate; hash panics.
- TestZZFrontEnds: YAML and subst panic.
- TestZZInvalidText: wrong diagnostic.
- TestZZCap: 10001 findings return 10000 with no RZ-CFG-001.

Mutation proofs, all 16 killed (run.py), by these tests:
- M1, no surrogates: kills TestHugeNumbersView choice/* and exact/*, which proves the enum and const members, plus TestBoundOracle, TestHugeNumberLiterals and TestNumberWorkBounded;
- M2, no recover: TestValidatorPanicRecovered;
- M3, no tags: TestUniqueItemsNumbers distinct cases;
- M4, residue zero: TestBoundOracle numbers views and TestHugeNumbersView third;
- M5, no sticky digit: TestBoundOracle;
- M6, key ignores shift: TestUniqueItemsNumbers huge-exponent cases;
- M7, invalid text passed as written: TestInvalidNumberText;
- M8, no byte charges: TestNumberCharges and TestNumberWorkBounded;
- M9, result stops at the cap, and M9b, option ignored: TestMaxDiagnosticsOption and TestCollectorCapSignal;
- M10, B2 surrogate integral: TestBoundOracle;
- M11, long grid literal as written: TestHugeNumberLiterals long_exact;
- M12, multipleOf ignored, and M13, view bound removed: TestNumberModel and TestBoundOracle;
- M14, exact residue replaced by the pattern: TestBoundOracle and the differential test;
- M15, huge negative exponent misclassified: TestHugeNumberLiterals and TestUniqueItemsNumbers;
- M16, model built after compile: TestNumberModel.

Minor comment fix: comment-only, so no test applies.
